{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310845,"nonce":"m7KYLxd5SLMya13R8/5B9YscRyA=","title":"Workflow wyonihg3u attempted to extend LoopVectorizationPass to handle symbolic trip counts. The extension was technically correct but dead ...","message":"**Status: REVERTED.** Real prerequisite identified.\n\n\nPhase 1 added ~340 LOC to `compiler/src/ir/vectorization.rs` lifting the Symbolic/Bounded trip-count rejection in `vectorize_loop` and splicing a runtime `n_main = n \u0026 ~(VF-1)` main + scalar tail (memcpy-style trip-count split). The shape is right.\n\n\n**1. Zero of the three named target loops vectorize.** MIR dumps at O2 AND O3 of `KVCache.append`, `GQAttention.expandKvHeads`, `LocalTempSampler.sample` show no auto-vectorized loop bodies. Root cause: `check_unsupported_ops` at vectorization.rs:595 rejects every loop body containing `CallDirect`. `Tensor.get/set`, `array_set_f64/i64`, `adjusted()` all lower to CallDirect. The new path is unreachable on production code.\n\n**2. The bench was at the wrong opt level.** `LoopVectorizationPass` is registered ONLY at O3 (optimization.rs:1904). `rayzor run` hardcodes O2. Both before/after bench runs executed at O2 where the pass isn't constructed. Reported 1.028× raw / 0.996× trimmed numbers cannot be attributed to the change — pure noise.\n\n**3. Latent SSA hazards in the reverted patch** (masked by being dead code):\n\n- LCSSA: exit-block phi-incoming pairs not rewritten after redirecting predecessor `loop_info.header → tail_header_id`\n- `remap_epilogue_instruction` only covers Const/Load/Store/BinOp/GetElementPtr; Cmp/Select/Cast/Phi/GetField/Alloca fall through with colliding dest IrIds\n- `find_loop_bound_cmp` accepts Gt/Ge but `emit_aligned_bound` only aligns the upper bound — unsound for decrementing loops\n- `analyze_memory_accesses` still hardcodes stride=1 and IrType::I64 on Store\n- `update_induction_stride` breaks after the first Add-of-IV match\n\n**4. `LocalTempSampler.sample` is permanently out of scope.** Inner insertion-shift is stride-1 backward loop-carried memmove dep — semantically non-vectorizable regardless of compiler work. Insertion sort cannot be lane-parallelized.\n\n\nSymbolic trip-count handling is necessary but **not sufficient**. Before any of the named loops can vectorize, ONE of the following must land:\n\n**(A) Inline Tensor.get/set/array_set fast paths before LoopVectorizationPass runs.** If the CallDirect dissolves into raw load/store ops at MIR time, `check_unsupported_ops` accepts them. Touches the inliner heuristics + the MIR wrappers for the small accessor methods. Cleaner long-term.\n\n**(B) Extend `check_unsupported_ops` with a pure-CallDirect allowlist + effect summaries.** Mark Tensor.get/set/array_set_f64/i64 as pure no-alias-no-side-effect operations; the vectorizer trusts the marker and emits vector load/store equivalents around them. Faster to implement, more conservative.\n\nEither path THEN benefits from a symbolic-trip extension (the spirit of what wyonihg3u tried) — but the order is reversed. Inline/allow FIRST, then trip-count generalisation.\n\n\nEven if the path were live, the bench would have been wrong. `LoopVectorizationPass` lives at O3 in `optimization.rs:1904`. `rayzor run` defaults to O2 (commit 4096373). To measure any vectorization win, either:\n- Move the pass registration to O2 (after the inline/allow prerequisite lands), OR\n- Bench with `rayzor build` / `bundle` / `aot` which default to O2 already, OR\n- Add a CLI opt-level override to `rayzor run` for benching at O3.\n\n\nPer the workflow's recommended sequence:\n\n1. **Inline Tensor.get/set fast paths** (Option A above) — unlocks the entire `nue/*` tensor-access surface, not just for vectorization but for any future loop-body-aware pass. ~200-300 LOC in the inliner.\n2. **Re-attempt symbolic-trip vectorization** with the inline prerequisite landed — at that point the three target loops should actually be reachable. Re-use the spirit (but not the LCSSA-buggy implementation) of wyonihg3u's patch.\n3. **Register LoopVectorizationPass at O2** (or add `--opt-level O3` flag to `rayzor run`) so users see the benefit without a hidden flag.\n\n\nThe workflow proposal correctly identified vectorization as the \"next-perf-lever\" per the audit. But it skipped Phase 0 of the chain — the audit-of-the-audit: WHICH op shapes are vectorizable today, and what blocks production code from reaching that shape. The CallDirect-via-Tensor.get rejection is the gate. We attempted a downstream change before clearing the upstream gate.\n\nThe discipline going forward: when \"extend pass X to handle case Y\" is proposed, audit the pass's INPUT acceptance criteria FIRST on real workloads, not just on synthetic loops the pass was designed for.\n\n\nWorkflow `w2h7za07k` re-attacked the prerequisite chain and shipped two of the four planned commits:\n\n- **`56e110f` perf(stdlib): force-inline Tensor and array accessor MIR wrappers** — InlineHint::Always on Tensor.get/set/permute/slice/reshape/scale/transpose_last2 + array_push/pop/length. Peels ~200k cross-extern call frames per 24-token decode. **Measured 1.05× speedup** (16.0s → 15.2s wall, 0.805 → 0.811 tok/s, 5-run mean).\n- **`aa294e3` fix(vectorization): repair five SSA hazards** — LCSSA exit-phi rewrite + remap_epilogue_instruction full arm coverage + find_loop_bound_cmp Gt/Ge guard + analyze_memory_accesses stride+element_type threading + update_induction_stride iterate-all. Correctness-neutral because the path is still dormant.\n\n\nPhase 4 (register LoopVectorizationPass at O2) — would add per-loop pass overhead with zero vector ops emitted because four upstream gates still block real loops from reaching vectorization:\n\n- **G1 (commit `b53b1dd`): NaturalLoop::trip_count now populated** via `analyze_loop_trip_count` at loop_analysis.rs:424-435. Correctness-neutral and DORMANT — measured 0/300 loops at O3 produce `Some(TripCount::Constant)` because they reject at gates higher in the chain.\n- **G4 NEW (dominant blocker, fires BEFORE trip-count check): 205/300 loops reject as \"Loop has multiple exits\"** at vectorization.rs:310. Caused by `Tensor.set([i,h,d], …)` body — the per-iteration `[i,h,d]` Array\u003cInt\u003e literal allocates via `haxe_alloc` + 4× `haxe_array_push_i64` with an error-path successor outside the loop. Hits every nested tensor-index loop in nue/* (KVCache.append bb4/bb8/bb12, GQAttention.expandKvHeads bb1/bb5/bb9). Fix: kill the per-iteration index alloc — either scalar `Tensor.get3/set3` fast path (skip Array\u003cInt\u003e entirely) OR MIR-level array-literal-to-stack-buffer lowering.\n- **G5 NEW: 95/300 loops reject as \"No suitable induction variable\"** at vectorization.rs:332. Need induction-variable analysis to recognize more patterns.\n- **G2: check_unsupported_ops rejects effect-free helper CallDirects.** `rayzor_update_call_frame_location` (empty body) and similar instrumentation helpers fail the CallDirect check. Still relevant after G4 lands.\n- **G3 (variant): RoPE.apply and Attention.applyMask are single CallDirect wrappers** over Rust kernels (`rayzor_tensor_rope`, `rayzor_tensor_causal_mask_`) with NO Haxe-side loops — structurally out of scope for LoopVectorizationPass regardless of gates.\n- **G1-extension: current analyzer only handles Constant trip counts.** Even after G4+G2 close, only literal `0...64`-style loops populate; production loops use runtime `n`. Symbolic/Bounded trip-count extension required separately.\n\n\nWhole-binary dump of llama-chat at O3: **53 vector ops total, ALL inside hand-written SIMD4f_*/SIMD2d_* stdlib intrinsics. ZERO from auto-vectorization** via LoopVectorizationPass.\n\n\n`tools/llama-diff/bench.sh` invokes `rayzor run` which defaults to O2 since commit 4096373; LoopVectorizationPass is registered ONLY at O3 (optimization.rs:1904). **The bench harness cannot observe the pass at all.** Future bench attempts must use `rayzor run --tier 3` or `--preset benchmark`.\n\n\nBoth adversarial verifiers independently arithmetic-checked: the 1.05× delta is 100% attributable to Phase 1 (inlining peels wrapper frames). Phase 2 contributes zero ops in the binary today. The prompt's green threshold required \"2+ target loops vectorize\"; zero do. Yellow with re-scoped commit framing is the honest call; the inlining win + correctness-prep both ship clean.\n\n\nThe wepbd3dx7 hypothesis (multi-exit is OOM-throw-Unreachable paths) was wrong. wepbd3dx7's own Phase 3 attribution surfaced the real cause: **stale `IrBasicBlock.predecessors`** at vectorizer time. `find_loop_blocks` truncates the body because back-edge predecessors aren't cached; `find_exit_blocks` then flags ordinary in-body Branch successors (terminator = Branch, not Unreachable) as exits. wepbd3dx7 helper-patch was a no-op (histogram before == after).\n\n**G4-recompute fix (`16e297f`)**: add `IrControlFlowGraph::recompute_predecessors` (~25 LOC in blocks.rs) and call it at `LoopVectorizationPass::run_on_function` entry (1 LOC in vectorization.rs). No signature ripple — the call sits where `\u0026mut function` is already available, not inside `LoopNestInfo::analyze` (which is `\u0026function`).\n\n**Histogram delta on llama-chat at `rayzor dump -O 3` (BLADE cache cleared):**\n- multi_exit:   210 → 70   (−140)\n- no_induction: 100 → 460  (+360)\n- Total visible rejections: 310 → 530 (more loops now reach analysis)\n\nThe shift is exactly the predicted shape: loops over-counted at the multi-exit gate now pass it and stall at the next gate (induction-variable analysis). **G5 is now the dominant blocker** (460/530 rejections). G4 is closed.\n\n**No auto-vectorization yet.** KVCache.append, GQAttention.expandKvHeads inner triples remain scalar in MIR. Reason is NOT G5 — they hit G2: `Tensor.get/set` lower to CallDirect (fn640381, fn640082, etc.) even after `aa294e3`'s SSA-hazard repair, which check_unsupported_ops rejects. The G2-prerequisite (effect-summary allowlist OR MIR-inline of Tensor accessor wrappers past the InlineHint::Always gate) is still required.\n\n**Correctness gates at commit:** 709 lib + 128/128 haxe + tiny-transformer PASS + llama-chat compare.sh \"What is the capital of France?\" 12 = byte-identical MATCH at O2 default. Build clean.\n\n**Bench:** not attempted at this commit — zero loops auto-vectorize, so any tok/s delta would be from `recompute_predecessors` analysis overhead (O(blocks × edges) per loop-vectorize-pass run), not from emitted vector ops. The patch is correctness-prep + gate-progress, not a perf win on its own. The 1.04× claim from wepbd3dx7's bench was bench-noise; this commit ships without one.\n\n**Caveat — fmt nit \u0026 pre-existing clippy noise:** the wt0duo218 regression gate ran `cargo clippy -p compiler -- -D warnings` which surfaced 7 pre-existing warnings in `rayzor-runtime` (unused fns `bias_to_performance_core`, `pthread_set_qos_class_self_np`, etc. — none from this patch). Confirmed by re-running clippy on a stashed tree. Workflow synthesizer (wt0duo218) over-fired red-revert on these unrelated warnings + a rustfmt single-line-closure nit on the new method. Both resolved before commit; patch is fmt-clean on its own files and clippy-clean on the compiler crate without `-D warnings`.\n\n**Next gate priority** (revised):\n1. **G2 (now dominant for nue/*)**: extend `check_unsupported_ops` allowlist with effect summaries for `array_set_f64/i64`, `Tensor.get/set/get3/set3`, OR lower these through a true inline pass that eliminates the CallDirect before vectorization runs. Either path unblocks ~50-100 stencil-shaped loops in nue/*.\n2. **G5 (now 460/530 of all rejections)**: extend induction-variable detection to recognize linear IV-of-loop patterns in the post-multi-exit cohort. Many of the 460 are likely simple-stride loops the analyzer just doesn't pattern-match.\n3. **G1-extension (Symbolic/Bounded trip counts)**: still required even after G2+G5 close — production loops use runtime `n`, not literal constants.\n\n\nPer wd10u3bui scoping memo recommendation, attempted P2 (pre-vectorizer MIR-inline pass) over P1 (allowlist + extend analyze_memory_accesses). 680 LOC at `compiler/src/ir/tensor_access_lowering.rs` with three-gate conjunctive guard:\n1. Index = single `i64` push onto indices Array\n2. Tensor.dtype proven F32 via factory `DType.F32` const-0 enum tag\n3. Intra-function reverse-in: factory dominates the access AND tensor register not reassigned\n\n**Outcome: ZERO effectiveness on real code.**\n- llama-chat O3 MIR: VLoad=0, VStore=0, unblocked_loops=[]\n- Histogram drift: multi_exit 70→75 (+5), no_induction 460→470 (+10) — slightly worse\n- Both adversarial verifiers refuted\n- Correctness GREEN (710 lib + 128/128 haxe + tiny-transformer + llama-chat MATCH at O2 default) — revert is purely an effectiveness call\n\n**Structural root cause**: The gate triple-AND is never reachable from real source. `InliningPass` + CFG construction split the factory + indices alloc + `Tensor.get/set` + dtype-const across SEPARATE basic blocks. Intra-function reverse-in finds none of them in the same function. Even smoke `var t = Tensor.zeros([4], F32); t.get([0]);` does not trigger.\n\n**Secondary correctness gaps** flagged by verifiers but never fired due to gate dormancy:\n- Gate 2 proved dtype==F32 but NOT ndim==1 — 1D literal index on N-D tensor would silently mis-address\n- Gate 3 did not prove non-null receiver — would have broken runtime's `null receiver → 0.0 / no-op` contract\n\n**What this teaches**: P2 (the structurally cleaner path from the scoping memo) was *correct in shape* — lower the call before vectorization rather than allowlist it — but **wrong in placement**. Two viable rebuilds:\n- **(a) Post-InliningPass peephole**: register the pass AFTER InliningPass has merged factory + indices + access into one block. Then intra-function reverse-in works.\n- **(b) Interprocedural dtype/shape summary**: lift Tensor.zeros/ones/etc. signatures from stdlib metadata into a summary table the lowering pass consults at any call site, regardless of CFG locality. Bigger refactor but works at any pass placement.\n\nNeither is a trivial follow-up. Both are bigger than the 680-LOC peephole that just reverted.\n\n\nw8u5f1ard's audit (15-25 samples from the 460 no-induction rejections) found 87.5% were \"canonical-but-rejected\": loops with phi-shaped IVs matching the analyzer's stated criteria but failing detection anyway. Audit pinpointed the root cause: **phis live in `IrBasicBlock.phi_nodes: Vec\u003cIrPhiNode\u003e` (the dedicated field at blocks.rs:27), NOT as `IrInstruction::Phi` variants in `block.instructions`**.\n\nVerified structurally: the entire Haxe-MIR pipeline (`builder.rs::add_phi`, `lowering.rs::add_phi_incoming`, `inlining.rs:cont_block.phi_nodes.push`) constructs phis exclusively via `phi_nodes.push`. **Zero constructors of `IrInstruction::Phi` exist in the codebase.** The inline variant exists in the type definition but no production code emits it.\n\n`find_induction_variable` at vectorization.rs:409 scanned `block.instructions` for `IrInstruction::Phi`. Guaranteed empty match for any Haxe-compiled function. Every loop tripped the \"No suitable induction variable found\" gate regardless of actual IV shape.\n\nw8u5f1ard's first 213-LOC implementation missed the structural fix — it tightened `is_simple_increment` + widened block scan but kept reading `block.instructions`. Zero histogram movement, red-revert.\n\nManual follow-up fix in commit `385b82e`:\n- Second scan over `header_block.phi_nodes` in `find_induction_variable`\n- New `is_const_step_increment` helper requires the non-IV operand to be a literal `Const` (defends against reduction accumulators being misidentified as IVs)\n- Kept the legacy inline-Phi path for backward compat\n- ~79 LOC net\n\n- **no_induction:  460 → 230  (−230, −50%)**\n- **no_mem_access:   0 → 230  (+230, newly visible next gate)**\n- multi_exit:      70 → 75  (+5, marginal drift)\n- unsupported-op:   -  → 10  (the G2 gate, now visible)\n\n230 loops pass G5 but stall at G3 (`No vectorizable memory accesses`). The stride analyzer at vectorization.rs:563-626 walks GEPs back to IVs; the 230 newly-visible loops have non-GEP memory access patterns (calls into `array_get_f64`, `rayzor_tensor_get`, etc.). This is essentially **G2 (CallDirect-as-mem-access) showing up at G3** — same bug, different gate.\n\n- 709 lib + 128/128 haxe + tiny-transformer PASS\n- llama-chat compare.sh \"What is the capital of France?\" 12 — byte-identical to llama.cpp at O2 default AND O3 (via `RAYZOR_OPT_LEVEL=3 rayzor run`)\n\n`RAYZOR_OPT_LEVEL=0|1|3` env var added to `run_file` (src/main.rs). Defaults to O2 unchanged. Verification scaffolding for O3-only passes.\n\n\nArchitectural premise of v2 vs v1 (wy360ho6y):\n- v1 was placed too early; InliningPass had not yet merged factory + indices + access; intra-function reverse-in gate matched nothing.\n- v2 placed at optimization.rs:1903, AFTER InliningPass (1888), ConstantFolding (1893), CopyProp (1894), GVN (1898), CSE (1899), LICM (1900), LoopUnrolling (1902). BEFORE LoopVectorizationPass (1904).\n\n**Scope phase findings (valuable even though impl red-reverted):**\n- Tensor.zeros (`compiler/src/stdlib/tensor.rs:520-546`, defaults to `InlineHint::Hint`) IS inlined into the caller after InliningPass at O3. Smoke confirms: `Test.main bb3` shows `extract_array_ptr_len` body + `call rayzor_tensor_zeros(data, len, dtype_ord)` directly visible.\n- Tensor.get / Tensor.set are `InlineHint::Always` (commit 56e110f). Inlined into caller. Wrapper itself gone from MIR — only the runtime extern `@rayzor_tensor_get` remains as a CallDirect inside the caller body.\n- DType.F32 lowers to ordinal `0i64`. The dtype-proof source is the DType arg of the factory call (last positional), const-folded back through copy-prop/gvn history.\n- Smoke MIR pattern AFTER InliningPass: bb2 = haxe_alloc(32) + 4× header stores + 1× haxe_array_push_i64(arr, iv) ; bb7 (immediate successor) = `Load(arr)` data_ptr + `Load(arr+8)` len + `call rayzor_tensor_get(tensor, data_ptr, len)`. The match-shape is recoverable across two adjacent blocks dominated by the alloc.\n\n**Why impl failed**: Implementation ballooned to **1202 LOC** (4.3× design estimate of 280 LOC), enforcing 8 hard gate predicates including a 3-iter dtype lattice with 8 hops Copy/Cast/BitCast tracing, intra-function reverse-in for non-null proof, exclusion of permute/slice/transpose_last2 from the dtype-preserving lattice (per stride-1 safety), etc. On the smoke test (`var t = Tensor.zeros([4], F32); for (i in 0...4) sum += t.get([i]);`) the pass did NOT fire — `diff /tmp/g3_smoke_mir.log /tmp/g3_smoke_post_mir.log` returns empty. Pre-fix and post-fix MIR are byte-identical.\n\nLikely culprits per smokefire.notes:\n1. Receiver `$20` is a phi in the loop's preheader-fed path; dtype lattice couldn't trace through it back to Tensor.zeros even though semantically it's invariant\n2. Some gate (G_inlined_shape walking backward in same block) over-strict about block boundaries when the pattern crosses bb2 → bb7\n\n**Lesson**: Even with smoke pattern visible AND correct placement AND correct dtype-proof strategy, the gate ENFORCEMENT can over-reject. v3 (if attempted) must include a SMOKE-FIRES TEST AS A UNIT TEST in compiler/src/ir/tensor_access_lowering.rs before any gate is enforced — match-and-count-only mode that prints \"would-fire\" without rewriting, validated against the smoke MIR first.\n\nThe smoke-test-not-firing scenario was caught by the v2 workflow's Phase 5 SmokeFire abort gate. Good.\n\n\n1. **GPU Tier 2 via existing rayzor.gpu infrastructure** — auditing in `weqk65ynn`. If existing GPU API can carry copyLastDim/broadcastRepeat with low new-code overhead, this is the highest-ROI lever for the named hot loops. Sidesteps the gate chain entirely.\n2. **CPU Tier 1/2 (multi-arg get/set + kernel ops)** — direct stdlib additions, no compiler changes. ~100-200 LOC total. Guaranteed to land. Drop-in replacement for `tensor.get([i,h,d])` patterns.\n3. **G3/G2 v3** — if pursued, must have unit-test-driven matcher BEFORE full gate enforcement. v2 lesson: over-strict gates with no fires-on-smoke verification waste 1200 LOC.\n2. **Downstream vectorization sites at vectorization.rs:696, 1300, 1470** also scan `block.instructions` for `IrInstruction::Phi`. For real auto-vectorization to emit, these need parallel `phi_nodes`-aware variants in the rewrite/clone logic. Currently latent, masked by the G3 stall.\n3. **G1-extension (Symbolic/Bounded trip counts)** — still required for runtime-N loops even after G2+G3 close.\n\n\n- [[bugs-known]] — O2 default landed but vectorization remains O3-only\n- [[project-qmatmul-threaded]] — the perf audit that identified non-matmul Haxe-side share\n- [[project-kernel-parallelism-phase2-reverted]] — prior parallelism-extension attempt that also red-reverted on wall-clock noise\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_loop_vectorize_symbolic` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}